#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:1
msgid "Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`--out` / `-o` says where. What lands there depends on the **profile**, "
"and two independent flags modify it. All three are settable from any "
"configuration source, not only from the command line — "
"{doc}`../../reference/configuration/options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:7
msgid "The three profiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:9
msgid "`regular`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:10
msgid ""
"the default. A directory, one CSV per table, plus "
"`investments_add_infos.yaml` for the details that belong only to bonds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:13
msgid "`single_file`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:14
msgid ""
"the path is a *file*, not a directory: one CSV with the investment "
"columns plus `Maturity` and `Interest rate` folded in. Only investments "
"are written; the other tables have nowhere to go. If the path does not "
"end in `.csv`, `out.csv` is appended to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:18
msgid "`structured`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:19
msgid ""
"a directory holding `investments/table.csv` and `investments/dicts.yaml`."
" Only investments, for the same reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:22
msgid ""
"Two of the three write only investments. That is not a limitation of "
"those profiles so much as what they are *for*: they exist for consumers "
"who want one artefact per run, and a fund table has nowhere to go in one "
"file without inventing a join."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:26
msgid "The tables of the regular profile"
msgstr ""

