#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:42
msgid "Three rules across every profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:44
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"They exist so a consumer never has to guess, and they are invariants of "
"the *product*: an output file that violates one is wrong even if every "
"step that produced it was right ({doc}`../../reference/design/entities-"
"and-output`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:48
msgid ""
"**every CSV always has its header**, even with no rows. A table with "
"nothing in it is a header-only file, never a missing one, so \"no rows\" "
"and \"no file\" stay distinguishable;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:50
msgid "**headers are exact**, in text and in order;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:51
msgid ""
"**an absent optional value is an empty cell** — never `None`, never "
"`null` — and a floating-point number always carries at least one decimal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:54
msgid "The two output flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:55
msgid "`--archive` / `-z`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:57
msgid ""
"Additionally writes a compressed **sibling** of the output: `.tar.gz` for"
" the directory profiles, `.gz` for `single_file`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:60
msgid ""
"Whether the uncompressed output is then removed depends on whether it "
"**already existed before the run**, checked before anything is written: a"
" directory you already had is never deleted. A path given as `-o "
"results.tar.gz` switches the flag on by itself and the suffix is "
"stripped, so it means the same as `-o results -z`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:65
msgid "`--separate-out`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:67
msgid ""
"Splits the two tables that carry a report per row — `investments` and "
"`funds_assets` — into one file per report:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:75
msgid ""
"The other tables stay merged, because they do not carry that column and "
"splitting them would mean inventing an attribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The document's **name** becomes part of the file name. A document left "
"unnamed defaults to its whole absolute path, and a path contains "
"separators, so `--separate-out` on an unnamed document tries to write a "
"file whose name is a path and fails. Name your documents — `-i "
"report.pdf:EURIZON 2023` — whenever this flag is on. See "
"{doc}`documents`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:85
msgid "One run, one set of tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/output.md:87
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Results from every page, every document and every job of the run "
"accumulate and are written **once**, at the end. Two documents in one "
"invocation share promise resolution and fund deduplication; the same two "
"documents in two invocations do not, and concatenating the results "
"afterwards is not equivalent. "
"{doc}`../../reference/design/multidocument`."
msgstr ""

